  "answer": "The goal was not met. Only one challenging case was confirmed: scene 02eadd92 at 0.8x speed with the crossing bus arriving 1.5 s late (S7), where every repeat failed. No other scene produced a single failure. On 02eadd92 the cause is not really the speed and timing combination. The route says turn right, but the policy drifts left into the bus's lanes and hits it head-on, or drives off the left edge of the road. This happened at almost every speed and timing tried, but outside S7 each setting was run only once or twice, so those are hints, not rates. Every failure is flagged as a possible simulator artifact because the ego ended far from the recorded path. The triage says the drift began before the camera view smeared and puts the fault on the policy, but rendering's part can't be fully ruled out.",
